# <%= it.scope %>/url-factory

[`@mfeflow/url-factory`](https://www.npmjs.com/package/@mfeflow/url-factory) under the company's scope, with
nothing added: the same `defineEndpoints` and `createUrlFactory`. It exists so apps import every shared package
from <%= it.scope %> and never from ours, and so <%= it.scope %>/http has something of yours to build on. It is
the place to add a company-wide helper later.

```ts
import { createUrlFactory, defineEndpoints } from '<%= it.scope %>/url-factory';

const endpoints = defineEndpoints({
  getOrder: { service: 'orders', path: '/v1/orders/:orderId' },
});
const bases = { orders: 'https://orders.example.com' };
const url = createUrlFactory(endpoints, (service) => bases[service]);
url('getOrder', { params: { orderId: 42 } });
```

## Settings only, no state

`<%= it.scope %>/url-factory` is not a Module Federation singleton, so every remote gets its own copy of this
package. That is fine while it only re-exports and builds things. Keep it that way: no module-level state here.
